  "worked_solution": "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(3\\,|\\,4)=P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=4).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=3\\,|\\,X=4)=\\frac{P(X=4,Y=3)}{P(X=4)}=\\frac{f(4,3)}{{f}_{X}(4)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(4) & =f(4,1)+f(4,3)+f(4,5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{8}{27}+\\frac{2}{27} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(4,3)=\\frac{8}{27}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{X}(4)=\\frac{13}{27}$ and $f(4,3)=\\frac{8}{27}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(3\\,|\\,4) & =P(Y=3\\,|\\,X=4) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(4,3)}{{f}_{X}(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{27})}{(\\frac{13}{27})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
